  "reference_solution": "SELECT customer_id,email,updated_at FROM customer_updates WHERE customer_id IS NOT NULL QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY updated_at DESC NULLS LAST, record_id DESC)=1",
  "solution_explanation": "Filter invalid business keys, partition by the key, and encode the complete precedence rule. Ranking a timestamp alone leaves tie behavior undefined.",
  "hints": [
    "Separate business key validity from precedence.",
    "Timestamp order is incomplete without a tie breaker.",
    "Use an explicit NULL order and stable secondary ordering per key."
  ],
  "senior_review": "Check deterministic precedence, NULL email preservation and replay stability; do not silently invent source uniqueness.",
